{
  "beruf": "lager-logistik",
  "title": "Warehouse and logistics",
  "level": "A2–B1",
  "reviewed": false,
  "_note": "italian-for-work run, 2026-11-15: written by hand for Italy, not yet read by a human or a second reader. translations.en = English meaning; deHint = German translation. Working conditions are general orientation only; facts marked 'to verify' in the run report.",
  "intro": "Warehouses and logistics hubs in the Po Valley (around Milan, Piacenza, Bologna, Verona), in Lazio and Campania hire many newcomers, often through an agenzia interinale (temp agency) or a cooperativa. This deck has the warehouse and its machines, picking and packing, goods in and dispatch, safety, and how to talk with your team and the agency. Colleagues usually say tu; with a manager you start with Lei until they offer tu.",
  "introEasy": "Do you work in a warehouse in Italy? Learn the words for your work here.",
  "jobs": [
    "Magazziniere/a",
    "Addetto/a alla preparazione degli ordini",
    "Mulettista",
    "Operatore/trice di logistica",
    "Addetto/a all'imballaggio"
  ],
  "tipps": [
    "Learn the numbers and the location codes first: «corsia dodici, scaffale quattro, ripiano due». You will hear them or see them on the scanner all day.",
    "Lift with your legs, not your back, and don't lift alone what is too heavy: «Mi dai una mano? È troppo pesante.»",
    "Driving a forklift (carrello elevatore) needs specific training with a certificate, often called patentino (requirements to verify). If you are asked to drive without it, say so: «Non ho il patentino per il muletto.» Ask the employer, a union (sindacato/patronato) or the Ispettorato del lavoro; this is general orientation, not legal advice.",
    "Your contract follows a national collective agreement (CCNL, for example logistics, transport and shipping). It sets things like shifts, overtime and breaks, and these rules vary: ask the employer, a union (sindacato/patronato) or the Ispettorato del lavoro; this is general orientation, not legal advice."
  ],
